    "knowledge_point": "Determining the Convergence of a Geometric Series With an Arbitrary Starting Index",
    "problem": "Which of the following statements is true regarding the series  ${\\sum }_{n=4}^{\\infty }{(-0.3)}^{n}$ ?",
    "worked_solution": "The series starts with $n=4.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{5}}{{a}_{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(-0.3)}^{5}}{{(-0.3)}^{4}} \\\\  & =-0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$",
